WEBVTT

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.610
Nicolo. Do you know how iron is made?

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.440
Yes, Minister Louis.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.400
They dig a hole in the mountain,

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.030
mine for rocks called iron ore

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.030
and burn them to make iron.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.290
Four thousand years ago...

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:23.210
...that's when the first iron
was invented in the Far East.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.040
The creators of iron sought
for a more suitable environment,

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.630
so they traveled west as they polished
their iron manufacturing technology.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.420
And finally,

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.590
they discovered a mountain
packed with the finest iron ore

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.680
in the territory of the Balt Empire.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.320
Now here's a question for you.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.860
The creators of iron settled those lands,

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.360
and kept their advanced iron-manufacturing
technology exclusive to them.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.330
Now, who were those people?

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.620
I know, the Rod Orm!

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:20.010
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.720
MARCH 27TH, TORQYEAN CALENDAR YEAR 76
EARLY MORNING, CHIELO, HAUBIA GATE

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.510
The gates are about to burn down.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.680
General Frentzen, the fire seems
to be dying out in the castle.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.430
-Perhaps this is our chance to reenter?
-No, Wachter.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.560
It's obvious

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.980
that they've got something prepared for us.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.320
How smart, they're not moving at all.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.440
Close the stone gates!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.710
I'm sorry.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.170
Looks like we're back
to square one, Mahmut.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.670
No, Director.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.100
Chielo's preparedness to repel
such a monstrous army

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.680
will, without a doubt,

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:29.060
propagate anti-Imperialist momentum
all over the continent.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:34.190
General Pino, 12th Division lost
a quarter of the provisions

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.400
they were transporting.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.570
If this stalemate with Chielo continues,

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:42.070
we are the ones who will likely run out
of our provisions first.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.070
Not to worry.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.790
There's plenty of food at Torqye's camp.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.080
The 22,000 soldiers of 4th Division,
not involved in the siege,

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.040
shall come with me!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.920
We'll destroy the 26,000

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.710
of the Torqyean army behind us!

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.880
2ND DIVISION LAND ARMY
LIEUTENANT GENERAL ANTON ADAM

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.380
5000 of 2nd Division!
5000 of 6th Division!

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.180
6TH DIVISION LAND ARMY
LIEUTENANT GENERAL GILBERT KIRCHHERR

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.470
5000 of 8th Division!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.390
8TH DIVISION LAND ARMY
LIEUTENANT GENERAL ALOYS REUS

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.640
5000 of 13th Division, 2000 of 14th Division!

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.810
13TH DIVISION LAND ARMY
LIEUTENANT GENERAL TRISTAN BARRETT

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.180
Making it a mixed unit of 7000!

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.100
In addition, while I am absent from headquarters,

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.270
I appoint Lieutenant General
Johann Frentzen

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.860
of First Army to take my place as commander.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.070
I will fulfill my duty no matter what it takes.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:25.870
Hey, Frentzen.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.120
Barrett's 13th Division

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.910
is only made up of military engineers, right?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:33.870
That's right.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.590
It's a craftsman group that specializes
in controlling and managing siege engines.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:42.050
Never imagined they'd be used in field battle.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.010
Could this be

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.010
another tactic from her?

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:54.190
In any case, all you have to do
is focus on the siege.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.560
But don't work yourself too hard.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.230
You too, Adam.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.030
Your duty is to support General Pino for all of us.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.700
Well look at that, they started to move.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:10.990
They're gonna take on the Torqyean Army,
the easier target.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:13.540
What do you think, Padrone?

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.580
The Torqyean Army has the greater numbers, but...

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.590
We should've had them come inside the castle.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.170
Being greater in number will suffice.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:25.130
The Empire's infantry and Torqye's cavalry...

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.930
...if they battle under the same conditions
on a prairie,

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.050
the favorable side is clear.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:35.100
Plus, we don't even know if they'll ever
reach Halil Pasha's main force.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.480
So what do you think, Halil Pasha?

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.690
Well, of course.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.820
We must run!

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.700
If we outrun the Imperial Army,

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.620
we could avoid conflict and win!

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.540
All right, then.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.590
First, let me do what I can,

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.000
Mahmut.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.340
8 DAYS LATER
APRIL 4TH, TORQYEAN CALENDAR YEAR 76

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.180
General Pino.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.970
As expected,

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:14.390
the Torqyean Army has been maintaining
a distance of two days from us.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:18.390
The enemy commander is Sehir Halil Pasha.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.400
He's chosen to avoid conflict as expected.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.530
Will our infantry

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.820
be able to capture a cavalry
so advanced in locating their enemy?

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:31.240
You're sure about this?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.830
I have no doubt about it.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.990
BALT-RHEIN EMPIRE CHANCELLOR'S SECRETARY
LILLI KOKOSCHKA

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.910
3 DAYS LATER
APRIL 7TH, TORQYEAN CALENDAR YEAR 76

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.830
Halil Pasha!

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:43.000
We're clear. There's a river
on the way, but we can cross it.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:47.210
By noon, we'll pass through the valley,
and get out to the next prairie.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.050
Where is the Imperial Army now?

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:54.220
Yesterday, their infantry was a full day
away from us to our north.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.310
There's no risk of confrontation.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.780
We're almost there.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.280
Our next camp site is a hillside in the south.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.700
I promise we'll feed you lots of grass there!

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.660
Halil Pasha.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:23.630
If we end up winning, it won't make for a very good story
after we return home.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:27.590
Let's hope so.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.530
Abbas,

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.530
I'm afraid you don't
have to worry about that anymore.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.660
Damn it, a river.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:57.240
They used a raft to shorten
the two days' worth of distance.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.960
But how did they know
we were going to pass through here?

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:05.840
Just by staring at the map,
she figured out the grassland areas

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.380
necessary to feed the horses and sheep
and located the Torqyean Army.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.170
Frentzen had prejudice towards her,

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.760
but she's not just some overseer.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:17.810
Shall we retreat?

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.060
No, no.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:22.850
It appears that the enemy
has a talented right-hand man.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.360
Even if we escape, they'll catch us soon enough.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.820
General Pino.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.940
Shall we settle our unfinished business

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.990
from 13 years ago right here?

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.910
We're the ones with the positional advantage!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.290
Let the battle commence!

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:45.040
I never expected to fight that formation again.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.460
That formation.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.500
I've seen it before.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.090
Good memory, Ahmed.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:55.180
The phalanx taught in Torqyean infantry drill

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:56.680
is an imitation of that.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.640
400 years ago against Urado,

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.770
80 years ago against the cavalry of Eru,

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.690
the Empire's moving fort,

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:12.150
an impregnable defense they developed after learning
from their many losses and struggles.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:13.780
Thirteen years ago,

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.200
Torqye was trampled down by that.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.660
But Ahmed,

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.870
it was Torqye who ended up winning that battle.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.250
Eighth Eyalet Army, Kurt Pasha.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.420
EIGHTH EYALET ARMY
KURT PASHA

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.210
Eleventh Eyalet Army, Kadoli Pasha.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.590
ELEVENTH EYALET ARMY
KADOLI PASHA

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.090
Your 8000 men will be in charge of the hunt!

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:44.140
Horse archers, advance!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:51.730
Horse archers!
They won't charge into us.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.030
Ruckenschild!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.210
Lancers, advance!

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.500
Release Ruckenschild, execute Schnabel!

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.010
The front line is tough.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.140
Lancers, retreat!

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.600
Horse archers, advance again!

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.310
Lancers retreat!

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.940
Execute Ruckenschild!

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.030
Halil Pasha...

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:40.740
thirteen years ago, you used the same tactic
to focus our attention to the front lines

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:45.290
while you sent out another squad
to attack us from behind.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.660
That's how you were able to devastate our army.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.830
But I refuse to make the same mistake.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.880
The weak point of our great formation

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.550
has been blocked by these cliffs this time!

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.760
You thought you executed an invincible formation.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:05.930
But this cliff isn't quite an obstacle for the Torqye!

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.640
The Eighth Eyalet Army's signal!

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.480
They've passed over the mountain.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.360
Six and Seventh Eyalet Army!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.190
Charge towards the formation!

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:23.120
Along with the Eighth and Eleventh
Eyalet Army coming from behind,

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.990
we'll surround the Imperial Army!

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.750
Lancers are attacking all at once!

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:31.330
Even the great formation won't...

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:36.380
Flugel!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.840
They cleared the way.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.220
They're luring us in

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.350
so they could encircle us.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.980
Our Hunters will be attacking them from behind.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.850
The Empire won't be able
to fully execute the encirclement!

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.860
There they are!
The last row of the formation!

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:59.530
Eleventh Eyalet Army!
Crush the formation from behind!

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.950
What is that?

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.160
Fire!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.840
Halil Pasha! The Hunters were ambushed!

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:20.760
Blume!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:22.970
No!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.350
Now the encirclement is complete.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.310
Well, what a surprise.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.480
Those weapons are normally used in capturing a castle.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.480
That's right, Kirchherr.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.610
Those ballistae are usually set around enemy territory.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:42.950
But they managed to disassemble and transport
the siege weapons here,

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.660
successfully utilizing them
in a field battle after reassembly.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.950
Eleventh Eyalet Army retreat!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.830
Leave it to us!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.420
We'll rescue Halil Pasha from the enemy's encirclement!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.750
Fire your arrows as you advance forward!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.960
Fourteenth Division, deploy!

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:13.980
You put Barrett in charge of 14th Division to guard
the military engineers with low offensive ability.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.940
You foresaw all of this.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.610
I respect your discerning eye,

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.400
General Pino!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.240
Focus all forces to the front!

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:28.070
We'll escape their encirclement!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.750
Without the military engineers,

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.540
we couldn't have transported those ballistae

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.000
or assembled them as rafts.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.960
That made up for the difference in mobility

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.970
between our infantry and Torqye's cavalry.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.180
Rescue Halil Pasha!

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.140
No! I can't get through!

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.600
Above all, Lady Kokoschka.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:59.270
Without your feat to analyze the map
and calculate the enemy's moves,

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:03.320
this ambush wouldn't have been possible.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:04.610
Oh, please.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.450
The one worthy of praise

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.820
is Minister Louis who established

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:13.490
Rumeriana's first military engineering unit, is it not?

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:15.950
At a battlefield,

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:19.210
our men have been faced
with the burden to dig tunnels,

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:24.670
build weapons, and create encampments.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.880
What if we were able to eradicate it all

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.300
so they could focus solely on the battle?

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.220
Our men would be ecstatic.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.100
In the process of mining

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:38.230
and converting rock to iron,

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.610
they attained the most advanced
engineering and construction skills.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:46.190
And that's the very weapon unique to the Empire.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:50.280
Hence why you built your new toy.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:54.580
Indeed. A military engineering unit led by the Rod Orm.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.790
The 13th Division.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.720
It's not over yet, Halil Pasha--!

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.220
Abbas!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.200
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.870
Seems like I was bested this time.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.420
General Pino.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.620
Distant Funeral Bells

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.590
APRIL 13TH, TORQYEAN CALENDAR YEAR 76
CHIELO

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.710
The Imperial Army's back!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.880
They're leading horses and sheep.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.380
Are those prisoners Torqyean soldiers?

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.970
The Torqyeans were defeated...

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.440
Those bastards.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.520
They're flaunting the commander's head!

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.530
8 DAYS LATER
TORQYE PASHALU, ALTU

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:55.660
The Imperial Army put up Halil Pasha's head,

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.910
and returned to their headquarters
outside the Chielo castle.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:02.960
Our expeditionary force was annihilated
by the Imperial Army's siege.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.670
They routed every last one of our men.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.630
The captives

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.710
were lined up in front of Chielo's besieged army

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:15.010
only to be beheaded one after the other.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:16.930
Buyuk Pasha!

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.470
You must send us to attack!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:19.640
KONDALGI DAWUD PASHA

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.220
I'll be the one who'll make the Empire pay

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.020
for what they did to our comrade, Halil.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.690
Buyuk Pasha, you must let us take care of it.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:32.730
We will not send any more Torqyean soldiers
to South Rumeriana.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.240
Cuore and South Rumeriana are entirely entrusted

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.450
to Halil Pasha and Mahmut Pasha.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.620
At this moment, we cannot be affected

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:44.830
by a single battlefield in the south.
It is a crucial time to make our best move.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:48.580
An indispensable figure of our country was killed!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.170
How could we ignore that?!

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:55.420
Without Halil, Torqye wouldn't have revived

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:58.390
after being devastated in the war 13 years ago.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:01.390
He invested materials for welfare and disaster relief,

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:03.640
and revived countless bazaars.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.890
Nobody loved Torqye and devoted themselves

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:09.350
to its prosperity and peace as much as Halil!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:13.230
Halil Pasha was defeated for that reason.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.490
For the past 13 years,

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.490
the Balt-Rhein Empire

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:22.030
made huge investments in its military and technology

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:27.290
while Torqye avoided wars and strived for peace.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:32.540
When the two extremes face each other in battle,
the victor is self-evident.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:36.300
You will not be able to defeat Balt-Rhein.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.220
However,

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:40.470
for the past 13 years,

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:44.930
I've only focused on how to win
the war against the Empire.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:48.940
I'll be the one

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.360
who'll crush the Balt-Rhein Empire itself!

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.030
Halil Pasha...

00:18:55.440 --> 00:19:00.320
I knew you weren't meant to live
in these troubled times.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.460
You would've been

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:16.210
a key figure after this war.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:20.010
Not me, or Zaganos Pasha.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.970
Hey, Mahmut.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.390
Don't you agree?

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.390
If we managed to return from this war alive,

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.190
it would've been nice to make the Pasha happy

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.770
by helping out with the reconstruction.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:38.990
But the Pasha won't let us repay him like that.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:43.160
He left the rest of the war
he couldn't end in our hands,

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:46.280
telling us to settle it.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.620
So we have to solve it.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:53.380
There's no other way for us to give back to the Pasha.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.000
We got our work cut out for us.

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.800
Right, brother?

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:14.860
You must be exhausted to have this thrown at you
so soon after becoming a Pasha again.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:23.910
Not at all. I can't be exhausted.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.530
Mahmut, you're a serious type.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:31.750
Are you thinking about this war?

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.210
Yes.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.830
I went back to being Pasha

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.210
so this wouldn't happen...

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:41.210
But I was useless once again.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.010
I'll always be...

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.800
always powerless...

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.430
without you...

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.600
Halil Pasha!

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.310
My aspirations, prayers

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:55.600
and wishes to be like you...

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:58.360
Without you...

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.240
Even then...

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:08.580
You just have to do whatever you can, Mahmut.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.870
There are many things

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:14.040
only you can make happen.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:16.290
Only me?

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:20.000
But you can't do it if you're crying like this.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.420
I'll go.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:05.420
I'll go and do what I can.

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:08.800
Off you go then.

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:50.490
Torqye's ray of hope.

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:52.490
In order to fulfill Minister Louis' visions,

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:55.030
I'll have to kill you now.

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:58.160
Next time, "Alliance Against the Empire."

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:02.000
You won't get away this time.
